      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4577_Start4" name="Strategy (VS-33); ESG/circular goal (VS-25/VS-73); category review">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4577_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4577_Task5" name="Merchandising/Circular Lead set the trade-in strategy &amp; scope (which…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Merchandising/Circular Lead set the trade-in strategy &amp; scope (which categories: power tools, appliances, equipment; trade-in vs buy-back; geographic/channel rollout), aligned to ESG (VS-25/VS-73)
Responsible (R): Merchandising / Circular Lead
Accountable (A): VP Merch
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4577_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4577_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4577_Task6" name="Finance/Merchandising build the program economics (trade-in-driven new-purchase…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Finance/Merchandising build the program economics (trade-in-driven new-purchase lift, refurbishment cost, resale margin, circular impact), and define success metrics vs do-nothing
Responsible (R): Finance / Merchandising
Accountable (A): CFO / VP Merch
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4577_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4577_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4577_Task7" name="Merchandising/ESG obtain approval, align to brand positioning…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Merchandising/ESG obtain approval, align to brand positioning (sustainability/affordability), and cascade to design (W4578–W4581)
Responsible (R): Merchandising / ESG
Accountable (A): VP Merch / CMO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4577_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4577_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4577_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
