    <bpmn:process id="W_W4579" name="W4579. Trade-In Valuation Engine &amp; Condition-Grading Model" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Trade-in inquiry; valuation rule update
Frequency: Per inquiry + periodic tuning
Volume: Valuations across eligible trade-in items
Owner: Merchandising (VS-01.2) / Service Center (VS-12.1) / Pricing
Participants: Stores (VS-07), Data (VS-28), Finance (VS-17.4)
Source: workflow W4579 — Trade-In Valuation Engine &amp; Condition-Grading Model</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4579_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4579_Lane1" name="Pricing">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4579_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4579_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4579_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4579_Lane2" name="Stores">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4579_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4579_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4579_Start4" name="Trade-in inquiry; valuation rule update">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4579_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4579_Task5" name="Pricing/Service Center build the condition-grading model (e.g…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Pricing/Service Center build the condition-grading model (e.g., A/B/C/for-parts) with objective criteria (function, cosmetic, age, battery/condition), and the valuation engine (grade × model × resale-value-minus-refurb cost)
Responsible (R): Pricing / Service Center / Data
Accountable (A): VP Merch
Duration: Annual + tuning</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4579_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4579_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4579_Task6" name="Stores/Service Center apply the grading at counter (inspect, grade…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Stores/Service Center apply the grading at counter (inspect, grade, system-generated valuation), presenting the trade-in value to the customer
Responsible (R): Stores / Service Center
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Per inquiry</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4579_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4579_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4579_Task7" name="Pricing/Data tune the valuation on resale/refurbishment outcomes (W4599)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Pricing/Data tune the valuation on resale/refurbishment outcomes (W4599), avoiding over/under-valuation, and refresh for model/age depreciation
Responsible (R): Pricing / Data / Finance
Accountable (A): VP Merch
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4579_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4579_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4579_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4579_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-695 (ensure controlled execution — Trade-In/Buy-Back Program Design, Valuation &amp; Pricing (PA-155.1).) | - CTL-695 (valuation = resale-value-minus-refurb-cost (W4582); grading objective/consistent; tuned on outcomes (W4599))
Owner: Merchandising (VS-01.2) / Service Center (VS-12.1) / Pricing</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
